\f0\fs28 I think the important issue wasn't 
\f4\i which derivative
\f0\i0  distinguishes special from general relativity.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 It was whether I would recognize the distinction between 
\f1\b local differential behavior and global relational structure
\f0\b0 .\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 And the torus supplies an especially powerful example.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 A flat torus can be constructed by identifying opposite edges of a Euclidean square.\cf0 \cb1 \
{\*\shppict{\pict {\*\nisusfilename MgIFB4FRbZnrpEVTSZL1WYgWUkzWKnyCQpCL8nwfItw_QeSD2jdqiXFK9HIXarfRQAovaDpN6W2Y8-EsF5zBhhvJFNhNNtBxUdX7rCdoqPpaIWOMRj3-3G9za7172OgelfbbRyndpZtUJEVTLxfi0FBKzsZQNtlURtTLO3__aCo}\picw695\pich473\picwgoal13900\pichgoal9460\jpegblip }}\
