\
\cf2 \cb5 Locally, that flat torus is indistinguishable from an ordinary Euclidean plane. Its intrinsic curvature vanishes everywhere. Yet globally, the two spaces differ: on the torus, certain paths wrap around and close. \cf0 \cb1 \

