\f0\fs28 \cf2 \cb5 \strokec2  is prediction error on a held-out future outcome.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 The critical experimental constraint: 
\f1\b both conditions receive the same pieces, the same computational budget, and the same prediction task. Only the availability or correctness of specified relationships changes.
\f0\b0 \cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 For example, suppose tomorrow you make an observation that connects something Aurora proposed today, something you said aloud yesterday, and a piece of code written three days earlier.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 The AI gets a chance to predict your next action.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 In one condition, it sees the three observations with their correct relationships.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 In another, it sees the identical observations, but their referential links have been withheld or carefully scrambled.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 If the correctly connected version predicts better, we've measured something the pile of observations alone didn't provide.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 Not consciousness. Not IIT's 
\f6\fs33\fsmilli16940 \cf0 \cb1 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f7 \cf2 \cb5 \uc0\u934 \cf0 \cb1 \

\f6 \cf2 \cb5 \uc0\u934 
\f0\fs28 \cf2 \cb5 \strokec2 . Not a proof of GPD. And not necessarily causal integration; observational relationships can improve predictions through correlation alone.\cf0 \cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 But 
\f1\b an operational measure of the additional predictive value carried by preserved relationships
\f0\b0 .\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 Introduce controlled interventions, compare counterfactual outcomes, and the experiment can begin testing causal dependencies rather than merely predictive ones.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 And here's the part I particularly like:\cf0 \cb1 \

\f1\b \cf2 \cb5 The model itself can become the object of the next experiment.
\f0\b0 \cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 Record its prediction. Observe what happens. Update its parameters. Then ask whether the updated model's next prediction depends on the relationship between its previous prediction, its error, and the resulting human response.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 Now we're testing whether preserved seams support 
\f4\i learning across experiences
\f0\i0 , not merely remembering them.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 The test recursively includes the learning process.\cf0 \cb1 \
\cf2 \cb5 That's a worthy checkpoint.\cf0 \cb1 \
